                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Knowledge Check</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why open with 1857?</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Argument</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">A model that works in 170 AD,</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"345\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">1857 Cleveland, 1985 Cupertino,</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"385\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">and 2024 your-office is not</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">a fad. It's a durable pattern.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"490\" width=\"940\" height=\"390\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"550\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cross-Century Evidence</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"610\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Marcus Aurelius: Danube frontier, 170 AD</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"655\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Rockefeller: Panic of 1857, age 18</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Steve Jobs: fired from Apple, 1985</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"745\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Patriots staff: Belichick era, 2010s</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"790\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Special Operations Forces: 2010s-now</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Same pattern, radically different domains.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Durability across centuries is the point."
