                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "title": "Quiz: Will at the Limit",
                  "question": "Why do the Stoics treat Will as the most important of the three disciplines?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "text": "Because perception and action are easy; only Will is hard",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Because everyone eventually faces obstacles that perception and action cannot remove — illness, loss, mortality — and only Will operates at that limit",
                      "correct": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Because the Stoics wrote about Will more often than the other two",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Because Will is the only discipline that requires courage",
                      "correct": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "explanation": "Holiday's structural argument follows the Stoics: every life eventually contains obstacles that perception and action **cannot remove**. The cancer diagnosis, the child's death, the irreversible loss, the certainty of one's own death. At that point, the operating discipline is Will — how you bear what cannot be removed, how you endure what must be endured. Marcus, Seneca, and Epictetus all wrote about Will because all three had needed it (lost children, exile, slavery). The other two disciplines are essential but bounded. Will operates at the limit, which is why it is the discipline that ultimately defines you.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Knowledge Check</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why Will is primary</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Perception + Action</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Essential. Powerful.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Bounded.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Fail when the obstacle cannot be removed.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"420\" width=\"940\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"480\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Will</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"540\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Operates at the limit.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Bears what cannot be removed.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"620\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">The discipline that defines you when nothing else can.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"660\" width=\"940\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"720\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why Stoics Wrote So Much About It</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Marcus lost children.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"820\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Seneca was exiled, ordered to die.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"860\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Epictetus born slave, permanently crippled.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Will is what's left when the other two have done all they can."
                  }
                }
