                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "question": "Holiday says the inside scorecard's most important function is:",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "text": "Helping you ignore criticism so you can focus on your dreams",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Letting failure inform you without letting it dissolve your identity or standard",
                      "correct": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Predicting which projects will succeed before you commit resources to them",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Replacing all external feedback with positive self-talk",
                      "correct": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "explanation": "The inside scorecard is **not** about ignoring criticism (option 1), nor a forecasting tool (option 3), nor a positive-thinking practice (option 4). Its function is the **separation** Holiday emphasizes throughout Part III: the outside verdict can be received as **information** without becoming **identity**. You can study the criticism, absorb the loss, and adjust the work — without letting any of it dissolve your standard or your sense of who you are. That separation is what Belichick maintained through both the effigies and the rings.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">The function of an inside scorecard</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"220\" width=\"900\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">SEPARATION</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Outside verdict → information</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"380\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Inside standard → identity</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"445\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Both true at once. Neither cancels the other.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"540\" width=\"900\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"595\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">NOT</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"640\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Ignoring criticism. Forecasting wins.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"680\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Positive self-talk.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"720\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">A discipline, not a mood.</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"800\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"855\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">THE TEST</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"905\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Receive the loss. Study it.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"940\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Standard still standing. Move.</text>\n                </svg>",
                    "caption": "Information without dissolution"
                  }
                }
